# Public Tenant Instagram Reel API

This endpoint returns the currently active Instagram reel configured for the tenant website.

## Get the active reel

```http
GET /api/tenant/reels/active
```

This is a public endpoint. No bearer token or visitor code is required.

## Headers

The endpoint does not require an `Authorization` header or `X-Visitor-Code` header.

The recommended header is:

```http
Accept: application/json
```

When the API serves multiple tenants and tenant resolution is based on a tenant-domain header, also send:

```http
X-Tenant-Domain: your-tenant-domain.com
```

Use the actual tenant domain configured by the platform. If the request is made to a tenant-specific API hostname, the tenant-domain header may not be necessary.

### cURL example

```bash
curl -X GET \
  "https://your-domain.com/api/tenant/reels/active" \
  -H "Accept: application/json"
```

Replace `your-domain.com` with the tenant's API domain.

### cURL with tenant-domain header

```bash
curl -X GET \
  "https://your-api-domain.com/api/tenant/reels/active" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-Tenant-Domain: your-tenant-domain.com"
```

## Successful response

When an active reel exists:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": "6f2a4b77-7d2a-4e0a-9f4c-123456789abc",
    "reel_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DU0g6-5iD3Y/",
    "is_active": true
  }
}
```

## Response fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | UUID of the tenant reel record |
| `reel_url` | string | Canonical Instagram reel URL |
| `is_active` | boolean | Indicates that the reel is currently active |

## Instagram URL normalization

Instagram URLs are returned in the canonical format:

```text
https://www.instagram.com/reel/{shortcode}/
```

For example, if the stored URL is:

```text
https://www.instagram.com/ila.homes/reel/DU0g6-5iD3Y/
```

The GET response returns:

```text
https://www.instagram.com/reel/DU0g6-5iD3Y/
```

The username path is removed. Existing canonical reel URLs are returned in the same canonical format. Non-Instagram URLs are preserved unchanged.

## No active reel

If there is no active reel, the endpoint returns a successful response with `data: null`:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": null
}
```

Frontend clients should handle this state by hiding the reel section or displaying a fallback.

## Frontend example

```ts
type TenantReel = {
  id: string;
  reel_url: string;
  is_active: boolean;
};

async function getActiveTenantReel(): Promise<TenantReel | null> {
  const response = await fetch(
    `${API_BASE_URL}/api/tenant/reels/active`,
    {
      method: "GET",
      headers: {
        Accept: "application/json"
      }
    }
  );

  if (!response.ok) {
    throw new Error(`Unable to load active reel: ${response.status}`);
  }

  const body = await response.json();
  return body.data as TenantReel | null;
}

const reel = await getActiveTenantReel();

if (reel) {
  window.open(reel.reel_url, "_blank", "noopener,noreferrer");
}
```

